TOOL RESULT tool_assess_symptoms: {'urgency': 'medium', 'doctors': [{'id': 'DOC-005', 'name': 'Dr. Argyris Fragkos', 'specialty': 'General Practice'}, {'id': 'DOC-007', 'name': 'Dr. Marco Bellini', 'specialty': 'Gastroenterology'}, {'id': 'DOC-013', 'name': 'Dr. Ingrid Svensson', 'specialty': 'ENT'}], 'raw_llm_response': "Medium. Sore throat, vomiting, and diarrhea can indicate a viral or bacterial infection (like gastroenteritis or strep throat) that often requires medical evaluation to rule out dehydration or more serious causes, but isn't typically an immediate emergency unless severe dehydration or other concerning signs are present.\n\nDoctor Specialties:\n1.  **Primary Care Physician (PCP) / Family Medicine:** Can diagnose and treat common infections.\n2.  **Internal Medicine:** Similar to PCP, focuses on adult illnesses.\n3.  **Pediatrician:** If the patient is a child."}
